bviz bundles and derives from the third-party work listed here. Each entry
gives what the work is, where it came from, and which licence declaration
records its terms. Every declaration names an SPDX kind and the text it
governs, so this file adds only what a declaration cannot state: which part of
bviz a work reached, and how. None of the terms below are bviz's own, which
are not settled, and nothing here grants any.

LICENSES/ holds the text of work bviz carries in its own tree. Work Bazel
fetches arrives with its own text, and its declaration points there.

## Compiled into the binaries

The fonts and the icon set are embedded with `include_bytes!` by //ui/assets,
so every binary built against it redistributes them and is bound by their
terms. Each is fetched with its own licence text, which the archive's BUILD
overlay in 3rd-party/ points its licence declaration at.

